{
  "requirement": "`fingerprint` identifies the version of the contents. `format` renders that same value for the agent.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait NodeContents: Send + Sync {\n    fn fingerprint(&self) -> Fingerprint;\n    fn format(&self) -> String;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has two obligations. `fingerprint` identifies the version of the contents. `format` renders that same value for the agent. The reviewed tests cover both.\n\n**Fingerprint identifies the version**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[structural_fingerprint_example_tracks_the_selected_function]` shows the fingerprint is equal for a reformatted function and differs when the function body changes. It asserts `assert_eq!` and `assert_ne!` on `fingerprint()`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[selected_contents_outlive_handles_and_later_file_edits]` shows the fingerprint stays the same after the file is rewritten and the original handle is dropped. It asserts `selected.fingerprint() == original`.\n- That test also pins the fingerprint's value and scheme to the structural hash and `{scheme}:own-v1`.\n\n**Format renders that same value**\n- The first test asserts `format()` returns \"second\" before and after the file edit. The fingerprint is unchanged at the same point, so both describe the same retained contents.\n- The second test asserts `format()` for the original, reformatted and changed functions. Each result is the exact selected text. The text differs exactly where the contents differ, and it is the text the fingerprint was computed over.\n\n**Trait shape**\n- The `shareable(&original as &dyn NodeContents)` call checks that the trait works as a `dyn` object and is `Send + Sync`.\n\nThe tests exercise the trait through `OutlineContent`, the SDK's shipped implementation. The other implementations of `NodeContents` that turned up in the search are test fixtures or `HabeasNodeContent`, which has its own requirements. I found no gap against the subject's text.\n\n`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` is also marked. It checks that the exports match the published API appendix, so it supports the trait's declared shape.",
